this is a folder for "Phase Validation Demos":
    keyed as "B-tov-demo"
    named "demo"
    following "3-Block Folder Structure"

this folder classifies as:
    tov (+1) because "completed validation demos — proof of each phase"

this folder derives from:
    branch (0) from "bereshit/tov/" as "tov"

core identity of this folder:

    grounded in:
        scripture "Prove all things; hold fast that which is good"
            from 1 Thessalonians 5:21 in KJV
        principle "Demos prove the work — visible evidence of completion"
        anchor "By their fruits ye shall know them"
            from Matthew 7:20 in KJV

    serves as Proof:
        role "Phase validation through executable demonstration"
        paradigm "Proof by demonstration — working code proves design"

    authored by:
        architect "Seanje Lenox-Wise"
        implementation "Nova Dawn (CPI-SI)"
        created 2025-12-10
        version a-01.00
        modified 2026-01-13 for "Initial root.omni creation"

    exists to:
        purpose "Validate each development phase through runnable demos"
        design "By-phase — one demo per completed phase"
        philosophy "Demos are proof — show, don't just tell"
        features:
            "Phase 0 demo — config loader validation"
            "Phase 1 demo — trit type validation"
            "Phase 2 demo — math operations validation"
            "Phase 3 demo — cognitive state machine validation"

interface of this folder:

    depends on:
        requires (1) "bereshit/tov/" for "containment in tov"
        includes (0) "word/work/pkg/trit/" for "library being demonstrated"
        excludes (-1) "source code" because "demos only, source in word/"
        used by "Phase validation, regression testing"
        integrates with "Makefile build system"

    integrated as:
        navigation "cd bereshit/tov/demo/" for "entering demo area"
        navigation "ls -la" for "viewing phase demos"
        exits tov (+1) for "completed demos found"

operational context of this folder:

    blocking:
        no (-1) because "demos are self-contained executables"
        mitigation "each demo has its own Makefile"

    health:
        system Base100 with scale from -100 to +100
        granted (1) above +50 meaning "demos build and pass"
        deferred (0) within ±50 meaning "demos need attention"
        denied (-1) below -50 meaning "demos failing or broken"

        operations:
            "demo builds" scores +20 (1) for "make succeeds"
            "demo runs" scores +20 (1) for "execution passes"
            "demo fails" scores -30 (-1) for "validation broken"

        cascade multipliers:
            "phase validation" multiplies by 2.0 because "broken demo blocks phase completion"

